hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19174","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mughira, from Musa ibn Ziyad ibn Hidhyam al-Sadi, from his father, from his grandfather Hidhyam al-Sadi, that he witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Farewell Hajj, and he said: Lo, your blood and your properties and your honors are inviolable to you as the inviolability of this day of yours and as the inviolability of this month of yours and as the inviolability of this land of yours."
"19175","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And Abu Khaythama narrated to me: Jarir narrated to us, then he mentioned the like."
